        "t1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Beverly Hills projects: the Flats, Trousdale and the canyons</strong></p><p>Beverly Hills divides at Sunset Boulevard. South of it, the Flats are level lots with deep backyards. The typical project there is a 60\" glass pool enclosure and a 48\" railing for a raised patio or a second-floor balcony. North of Sunset, Trousdale Estates and the streets off Benedict and Coldwater canyons climb the hills. Houses there are built around a view terrace, and a frameless glass railing is what keeps that view open.</p><p>Inside the house, remodels led by architects often replace a solid stair wall or wood balusters with custom stair glass in spigots. The hardware comes in Brushed Stainless or Matte Black. We ship all of it crated to the site: 12 mm tempered panels, 2205 stainless hardware, connectors for corners and a wall connector where a run meets plaster.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t2": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Hillside lots, fire zones and the 42\" rule</strong></p><p>The California code sets 42\" as the minimum guard height even for a single-family house. A pool enclosure must be 60\", with gaps under 4\" and a latch at least 60\" above ground. The City of Beverly Hills Community Development Department applies the 2022 Title 24 codes, and hillside lots north of Sunset have their own review. Parts of the canyons are mapped fire hazard zones. Glass and stainless steel do not burn, but ask the fire authority about the rules for the deck itself. Many Benedict and Coldwater canyon homes with a Beverly Hills mailing address sit in the City of Los Angeles, where permits go through LADBS. The <a href=\"/pages/california-building-standards-code-for-glass-railings\">California code page</a> has the summary.</p><p>Earthquake rules do not add railing requirements. What a plan checker looks at is the attachment, and our engineering documents cover the spigots on concrete and wood.</p>"
          }
        },
        "t3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Delivery to Beverly Hills and installation</strong></p><p>Orders are processed in 2–3 business days, then delivered in 5–10 business days by freight carrier with liftgate delivery. Custom sizes, including stair glass, take 2–3 business days to process and 2–3 weeks to ship. Order that glass early on a remodel schedule. The driver lowers the crate at the curb or in the driveway; on a narrow canyon road, tell us about truck access when you order. The price at checkout is final, with no duties, tariffs or hidden fees, and orders over 3,000 USD ship free. Report any damage within 3 days, before installation, for a free replacement or refund.</p><p>The system is designed for DIY installation. Most standard installations take about 4 hours with the <a href=\"/pages/glass-railing-installation-guide\">installation guide</a> and videos, and a contractor on site can follow the same guide. Spigots fix to concrete or wood with screws sold separately.</p>"
          }
        }
